round.resubmitted=Round {0} ({1}) was already created from this form; it was not created a second time.
round.resubmitted.attempts=Round {0} ({1}) was already created from this form; it was not created a second time. Its distribution was stopped after repeated crashes (reference {2}) and was not resumed: use “Retry” on its job once the cause is fixed.
round.resubmitted.resumed=Round {0} ({1}) was already created from this form; it was not created a second time. Its distribution was resumed.
round.resubmitted.distributing=Round {0} ({1}) was already created from this form; it was not created a second time. Its images are still being distributed.
round.still.distributing=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started yet: its images are still being distributed. It starts by itself once its distribution has finished.
round.start.state.not.distributed=Not started – waiting for distribution
round.start.state.distributing=Images are being distributed. The round starts by itself when done.
round.start.state.selecting=Not started – its images are being selected for review
round.start.state.incomplete=Not started – its creation didn''t finish
round.start.refused.not.distributed=Round {0} ({1}) hasn''t been distributed to jurors yet: it is still being set up. Its row shows the next step: “Check the files”, then “Distribute to jurors”.
round.start.refused.selecting=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started yet: its images are still being selected for review. Then choose its jurors and distribute its images.
round.start.refused.incomplete=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started: its creation didn''t finish. To finish it, edit the round, tick “Distribute ? new files” and save.
round.start.refused.retired=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started: its contest is retired.
round.start.state.cancelled=Not started – its creation was cancelled
round.start.state.failed=Not started – its distribution failed
round.start.refused.cancelled=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started: its creation was cancelled. To create it after all, edit the round, tick “Distribute ? new files” and save.
round.start.refused.failed=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started: its distribution failed. Retry its job in its row.
round.start.state.reapply.failed=Setting up – step 2 of 3: re-applying its filters failed
round.start.state.reapply.cancelled=Setting up – step 2 of 3: re-applying its filters was cancelled
round.start.refused.reapply.failed=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started: re-applying its filters failed, so its images are only partly selected. Retry its job in its row, or edit the round and re-apply its filters, then choose its jurors and distribute it.
round.start.refused.reapply.cancelled=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started: re-applying its filters was cancelled, so its images are only partly selected. Edit the round and re-apply its filters, then choose its jurors and distribute it.
round.start.refused.changed=Round {0} ({1}) wasn''t started: it changed meanwhile. Try again.
round.start.refused.incomplete.no.jurors=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started: its setup didn''t finish, and it has no jurors yet. Use “Find the matching files again” in its row, check its files, then choose its jurors and distribute it.
round.start.refused.cancelled.no.jurors=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started: its setup was cancelled before it had jurors. Use “Find the matching files again” in its row, check its files, then choose its jurors and distribute it.
round.find.again.failed.reference=Round {0} ({1}): its matching files couldn''t be found again (reference {2}). Try “Find the matching files again” once more; if it fails again, send the tool''s administrators (root) this reference.
round.find.again.failed=Round {0} ({1}): its matching files couldn''t be found again: {2}
round.find.again.refused=Round {0} ({1}): its matching files can''t be found again from here. Only a round whose setup was cancelled or didn''t finish, meant to be reviewed first and with no jurors, has this. Reload the Rounds page to see what it can do now.
round.find.again.running=Round {0} ({1}) already has a job running: wait for it to finish.
round.find.again.started=Round {0} ({1}): finding its matching files again. Then it waits for review: check its files, choose its jurors and distribute it.
round.find.again=Find the matching files again
round.start.refused.cancelled.no.jurors.new=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started: its setup was cancelled before it had jurors, and it was meant to be distributed right after its files were found, which needs jurors. Set up a new round instead.
round.start.refused.incomplete.no.jurors.new=Round {0} ({1}) can''t be started: its setup didn''t finish, it has no jurors, and it was meant to be distributed right after its files were found, which needs jurors. Set up a new round instead.
round.distribute.running=Round {0}: its images are already being distributed.
round.distribute.attempts=Round {0}: its distribution was stopped after repeated crashes (reference {1}) and was not resumed. Use “Retry” on its job once the cause is fixed.
round.distribute.running.files=Round {0}: its images are already being distributed. The listed files were not added: add them again once it has finished.
round.distribute.resumed.files=Round {0}: its failed distribution was resumed instead of adding the listed files. Add them again once it has finished.
