# criteria rounds (C2): the round form, the catalogue, and the shipped criteria (V83)
criteria = Criteria
criteria.help = For a rated round: {0} to {1} criteria from the catalogue, in their order, each rated on the round stars. A file is rated once all its criteria are, with their sum; with one criterion, the file''s rate is its stars on that criterion. None: a round without criteria. Criteria can''t be changed while the round is running or once it has votes.
criteria.locked = The round''s criteria can''t be changed while it is running or once it has votes.
criteria.locked.none = It has no criteria, and none can be added.
criteria.catalogue = Criteria catalogue
criteria.catalogue.help = The criteria the round forms of every contest offer. A criterion added here is named by its text in every language until it is translated. Criteria are not changed or removed here.
criteria.catalogue.added = Criterion added.
criteria.catalogue.full = The catalogue is full.
criteria.catalogue.exists = A criterion of this name exists.
criteria.position = Criterion {0}
criteria.form.add = Add criteria
criteria.form.add.another = Add another criterion
criteria.form.remove = Remove criterion {0}
criteria.single = Rate: {0}
criteria.name = Name
criteria.fallback.name = Text without a translation
criteria.add = Add criterion
criteria.add.name = New criterion
criteria.add.help = Its name, up to 255 characters.
criteria.overall = Overall, per criterion
criteria.sum = sum of the criteria
criteria.rate.one = {0} (Σ {1})
criteria.rate.many = {0} (Σ {1}: {2})
criteria.rate.sum = {0} (Σ {1}, sum of {2} jurors)
average.rate = {0} ({1})
average.sum = {0} (sum of {1} jurors)
average.denominator.jurors = {0} / {1} jurors
average.denominator.rated = {0} / {1} of {2} jurors
average.denominator.sum = sum of {0} jurors
round.average.rule = File score
round.average.rule.rated = Average over the jurors who rated it
round.average.rule.assigned = Average over its assigned jurors (unrated counts as 0)
round.average.rule.sum = Total of the rates (a file a juror skipped adds nothing)
round.average.rule.help = How a rated round scores a file in its results, its rankings and a next round''s minimum: the average over the jurors who rated it; the average over all its jurors, a missing rate counted as 0; or the total of the rates. Can be changed at any time; a next round already distributed keeps the files it took.
round.average.rule.of = File score: {0}
round.average.rule.change.warning = Saving a different score rule re-scores and re-orders this round''s results on every page, and takes effect at once: nothing is recomputed in the background. A distribution already queued or running keeps the rule it started with.
round.average.rule.change.later = {1,choice,1#Round {0} took its files by the scores of this round; those files stay. Distributing new files to it from now on uses the new rule.|1<Rounds {0} took their files by the scores of this round; those files stay. Distributing new files to them from now on uses the new rule.}
average.file.rating.sum = From a round scored by the total of the rates: a minimum score, the total (e.g. up to 50 for 10 jurors of 5 stars).
