# adding a juror with a fair share of the donors' unrated files (round_rebalance, PR 1b)
round.juror.add.donors.help=Ticked jurors give some of their unrated files to the new juror, so that they all end with about as many unrated files. Stopped jurors are listed unticked; a ticked stopped juror gives and stays stopped.
round.juror.add.unrated={0} unrated
round.juror.add.share={0} unrated files over {1} jurors. {2} gets about {3}: from {4}.
round.juror.add.share.none={0} gets nothing: no ticked juror has more unrated files than {0}.
round.juror.add.stopped.donor=A ticked stopped juror gives their unrated files and stays stopped.
round.juror.add.restart={0} is stopped in this round: the add starts them again, and they can then change their earlier votes in the round.
round.juror.add.restart.confirm=Start {0} again
round.juror.add.restart.subject=Juror to start again:
round.juror.share=Start and give a fair share…
job.error.rebalance.donor=Account {0}, ticked to give files, isn''t a juror of round {1}.
job.error.rebalance.already.juror={0} is already an active juror of round {1}: they can''t be added again.
job.error.rebalance.stopped.juror={0} is stopped in round {1}: start them again from the round statistics (Start and give a fair share…).
job.error.rebalance.donor.verify=Round {0}: juror {1} has lost another number of files than they gave. Retry checks again.
# reassigning a juror's unrated files (round_rebalance, docs/plans/2026-11-16-round-editing.md, step 3)
round.juror.reassign=Reassign files…
round.juror.reassign.of=Reassign {0}''s files…
round.juror.reassign.title=Reassign a juror''s files
round.juror.reassign.title.of=Reassign {0}''s unrated files in round {1} {2}
round.juror.reassign.help=The juror''s unrated files go to the jurors ticked below, so that they all end with about as many unrated files. Their votes stay as they are, in every view. Afterwards the juror is stopped in this round. The round must be running.
round.juror.reassign.counts={0} has {1} files in this round: {2} rated (✗ and partly rated included; they stay), {3} unrated, and {4} set aside (files deleted on Commons or disqualified).
round.juror.reassign.receivers=Jurors who receive the files
round.juror.reassign.receivers.help=The round''s active jurors are ticked. Stopped jurors are listed unticked: a ticked stopped juror is started again, and can then change their earlier votes in the round. A file goes only to a juror who doesn''t have it yet.
round.juror.reassign.show=Show what this does
round.juror.reassign.result={0,choice,1#1 unrated file|1<{0,number,integer} unrated files} → {1,choice,1#1 juror|1<{1,number,integer} jurors}: {2}.
round.juror.reassign.waiting={0} files can''t move (every ticked juror already has them): they wait for a juror. The round''s statistics show them, and “Distribute new files” can give them out.
round.juror.reassign.aside={0} unrated files set aside go to ticked jurors too ({1} of them; the others are removed), so that a file restored on Commons or requalified comes back to an active juror.
round.juror.reassign.all=Every file goes to every juror in this round: nothing is given. {0}''s {1} unrated files are removed from them; the other jurors have them already.
round.juror.reassign.restart=Started again by this: {0}. They can then change their earlier votes in the round.
round.juror.reassign.stop=Afterwards {0} is stopped in this round. Their votes stay. To bring them back, use “Start and give a fair share…”.
round.juror.reassign.confirm=Reassign {0}''s files
round.juror.reassign.queued=Reassigning {0}''s files in round {1}: queued. The job column below shows its progress.
round.juror.reassign.done={0}''s files in round {1} reassigned: {2} given, {3} waiting for a juror.
job.error.rebalance.reassign.not.running=Round {0} isn''t running: start it first. Files are reassigned only in a round open to its jurors.
job.error.rebalance.reassign.legacy=Round {0} has no list of jurors (an old round): its files can''t be reassigned.
job.error.rebalance.from=Account {0} isn''t a juror of round {1}.
job.error.rebalance.reassign.nothing={0} has no unrated files in round {1}: there is nothing to reassign. If they are still voting, pause them with “Pause the juror''s voting” in the round''s statistics.
job.error.rebalance.reassign.alone=Juror {0}''s files in round {1} can''t be reassigned: {2,choice,0#every file goes to every juror, and no other juror of the round is active with an active jury membership of the contest. Resume the voting of one, or add a juror with “Add juror…”|1#no other juror of the round has an active jury membership of the contest. Add a juror first with “Add juror…”|1<each file goes to {2,number,integer} jurors, and fewer than {2,number,integer} other jurors of the round have an active jury membership of the contest. Add a juror first with “Add juror…”} in the round''s statistics.
job.error.rebalance.receiver=Account {0}, ticked to receive files, isn''t a juror of round {1} with an active jury membership of the contest.
job.error.rebalance.receivers.few=Round {0} gives each file to {1,choice,1#1 juror|1<{1,number,integer} jurors}: tick at least {1,choice,1#1 juror|1<{1,number,integer} jurors} to receive files, or add a juror first.
job.error.rebalance.reassign.verify=Round {0}: juror {1} still has {2} unrated files. Retry checks again.
job.error.rebalance.receiver.verify=Round {0}: juror {1} has a different number of files than expected. Retry checks again.
job.error.rebalance.from.verify=Round {0}: juror {1}''s rated votes changed meanwhile. Retry checks again.
round.waiting={0,choice,1#1 file is waiting for a juror: it has|1<{0,number,integer} files are waiting for a juror: they have} fewer jurors than the round gives each file ({1}).
round.waiting.topup={0,choice,1#Also give out the 1 file waiting for a juror|1<Also give out the {0,number,integer} files waiting for a juror}
round.waiting.topup.help=Each gets its missing jurors from the round''s active jurors who don''t have it, the least loaded first. Off by default.
round.waiting.topup.resumed=Round {0}: its failed distribution was resumed instead, so the files waiting for a juror were not given out. Tick “Also give out the files waiting for a juror” again once it has finished.
round.juror.reassign.done.all={0}''s files in round {1} reassigned: every juror has every file in this round, so nothing was given; {2,choice,0#no unrated file was|1#1 unrated file was|1<{2,number,integer} unrated files were} removed from them.
round.juror.reassign.cancelled.partway=Reassigning was cancelled after {0,choice,0#none|1#1|1<{0,number,integer}} of the juror''s unrated files had been moved or left waiting: the juror (account {1}) stays stopped, and their other unrated files stay with them. Run “Reassign files…” again to move the rest.
round.juror.reassign.cancelled.removed=Reassigning was cancelled after {0,choice,0#none|1#1|1<{0,number,integer}} of the juror''s unrated files {0,choice,0#was|1#was|1<were} removed from them (every juror has every file in this round): the juror (account {1}) stays stopped, with their other unrated files. Run “Reassign files…” again to remove the rest.
round.juror.preview.stale=The ticks changed: click “{0}” first.
round.juror.no.membership=no active membership
round.juror.add.split={0} gets about {1,choice,1#1 file|1<{1,number,integer} files}: {2,number,integer} waiting + {3,number,integer} from others. Files waiting for a juror go to them first.
round.juror.add.split.from=From others: {0}.
round.juror.add.split.waiting={0} gets {1,choice,1#the 1 file|1<the {1,number,integer} files} waiting for a juror that they may take. Nothing comes from the others: no ticked juror has more unrated files than {0}.
round.juror.add.waiting.left={0,choice,1#1 more file waiting for a juror keeps|1<{0,number,integer} more files waiting for a juror keep} waiting: “Distribute new files” with “Also give out the files waiting for a juror” gives them out.
job.error.rebalance.invariants=Round {0}: {1,choice,1#1 file is|1<{1,number,integer} files are} out of step with their votes after the move (file {2} first). Retry checks again.
job.error.rebalance.invariants.count=Round {0}: {1,choice,1#1 more file is|1<{1,number,integer} more files are} out of step with their votes after the move than before it. Retry checks again.
# P3: jurors chosen before Distribute; re-apply filters (P3-5)
round.review.distribute.no.jurors = Round {0} has no jurors: choose them, then distribute.
round.review.distribute.too.many.per.file = Each file can''t go to {0} jurors: only {1} jurors are chosen.
round.review.distribute.jurors.locked = Round {0}: its distribution has started (it has votes), so its jurors can''t change now. Retry its job to finish it.
round.review.prev.changed = Votes in the previous round(s) have changed since these images were selected. Re-apply the filters (Edit the round) to select by the current votes, or distribute these images anyway.
round.review.prev.changed.confirm.box = Distribute anyway: the images as selected before the votes changed
round.review.prev.changed.confirm = Round {0}: votes in its previous round(s) have changed since its images were selected. Tick "Distribute anyway" to distribute them as they are, or re-apply the filters.
round.review.jurors.help = The jurors who get this round''s images. You can change them until you distribute.
round.review.distribute.jurors.help = Opens the round''s jurors form: choose the jurors and the file distribution there, then distribute.
