# joining accounts (the account join plan's J-2)
duplicates.join = Join…
wiki.taken.join = Join the two accounts…
account.join.title = Join accounts
account.join.explain = Joining keeps one account and retires the other: its contests, round assignments, votes, votes set aside and comments move to the account kept. Both accounts'' sessions end and their API tokens and unused links are revoked; the retired account''s Google or Wikimedia sign-ins are unlinked (their holder links them again from the account kept). It can''t be undone. A vote of both accounts on the same file in the same round refuses the join.
account.join.back = Back to the possible duplicates
account.join.keep.legend = Which account to keep
account.join.keep = Keep
account.join.keep.this = Keep {0}
account.join.keep.unverified = Another account has an email its owner proved: keep that one.
account.join.show = Show what joining would do
account.join.preview.title = Join {0} (#{1}) into {2} (#{3})
account.join.refused.intro = This join can''t start:
account.join.refused.collisions = {0} files have a vote of both accounts in the same round (listed below). Fix them by hand first: a join never drops a vote.
account.join.refused.kept.unverified = Account #{0} has an email its owner proved and this one hasn''t: keep #{0} instead.
account.join.refused.retire = Account #{0} can''t be retired by you: {1}.
